index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..a19ecee5bc10d51ba9a1a2f0ce29c16466983b35
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/preparation_shader_cache/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+# Semantic shader cache fixture
+
+Run `bash tests/preparation_shader_cache/run.sh` for the portable contract fixture.
+It compiles with C++14 and treats warnings as errors. The compile callback consumes
+actual verified original source/include bytes, allowing clean and cached build
+comparison without a GPU. The fixture covers nested local/system opens, explicit
+outside-tree dependencies, failed preferred candidates before CWD fallback,
+same-size and same-mtime edits, options/defines/compiler/ABI/patch identity,
+immutable compile replay after live mutation, missing/cyclic/alias rejection,
+checksum/truncation recovery, quotas, and reservation release.
+
+`windows.cpp` requires the installed Windows SDK's `d3dcompiler.lib`, plus
+`ShaderSourceCache.cpp`, `SnapshotIO.cpp`, and `RefreshCpuBudget.cpp`. Its single
+argument is a precreated empty owned directory. Use a lexical path with no
+reparse points, hard links, or distinct short-name aliases, as required by the
+production source watcher. It runs actual `D3DPreprocess`/`D3DCompile` with a
+counter, verifies byte-identical clean output, same-mtime include invalidation,
+compile-flag invalidation and cache-hit compile avoidance, then invokes the
+production adapter to verify its loaded-DLL compiler digest path. Eight more
+cases compare both preprocessed output and compiled bytecode against the real
+SDK standard include handler for LOCAL/SYSTEM at root/nested levels, root
+preference and CWD fallback. Cache hits skip the counted compilation callback.
+`standard_probe.cpp` is a standalone SDK probe for this search policy.
+The preflight on windows-2022 confirmed root preference for both include kinds
+and captured-CWD fallback even for nested parents.
+
+The production entry point is `PrepareD3DShader`. It is worker-only and retains
+original source quality. Preprocessing discovers actual conditional/macro
+include edges using verified snapshots; compilation replays exactly that sealed
+closure without filesystem access. Cached portable bytecode is accepted only
+after rediscovery and hashing all actual source/include bytes and options.
+Device objects stay in the existing device-epoch cache; no device/driver-specific
+artifact is serialized. `recursive_include=0/1` preserves the existing Migoto
+handler's identical LOCAL/SYSTEM search policy and nested-parent behavior.
+`recursive_include=-1` uses the SDK-qualified standard handler policy (initial
+source directory then captured CWD for either include kind). Non-ASCII include
+names in this standard mode remain compatibility-only until the SDK filename
+encoding is qualified; modes 0/1 retain legacy UTF-8 behavior. Cyclic graphs,
+unresolved input, nonwatchable aliases and compiler/preprocessor graph
+disagreement remain explicit compatibility cases. Unsupported HLSL syntax
+(such as macro names in include directives on this SDK compiler) keeps its
+legacy compilation failure; the fixture uses actual conditional literal
+includes and verifies inactive nonexistent inputs are never opened.
+
+The caller must add returned source snapshots and every `lookupPaths` candidate
+to the activation/invalidation closure, including missing earlier search paths.
+Legitimate `..` includes outside Mods are allowed and explicitly tracked. The
+caller supplies a shared CPU budget, captured working directory, and dedicated
+cache directory outside Mods, and retains the returned ownership tokens. An
+additional bytecode-copy lease is needed when creating an `ID3DBlob` copy.
+
+Limits bound source, closure, graph, bytecode, metadata reservations, cache
+entry count and disk bytes. The compiler's own private heap cannot be measured
+or capped by D3DCompile; a conservative admitted scratch allowance is retained
+while compiling and oversized compiler output is rejected. This fixture does
+not qualify game appearance, device-driver behavior, or frame timing.
